1
00:00:03,630 --> 00:00:07,064
Every company moving to SAP's cloud carries hundreds of custom

2
00:00:07,214 --> 00:00:09,215
ABAP programs written over fifteen years.

3
00:00:09,365 --> 00:00:12,799
Each one must be checked against Clean Core rules before

4
00:00:12,949 --> 00:00:16,742
it can move, and today that review is done by hand,

5
00:00:16,892 --> 00:00:19,610
by the few people who know both worlds.

6
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:23,911
I asked a narrower question than "can IBM Bob do this review":

7
00:00:24,061 --> 00:00:26,420
how well does it do it, measured?

8
00:00:26,570 --> 00:00:29,839
So I built the exam before the demo.

9
00:00:29,989 --> 00:00:34,541
Four synthetic legacy programs with forty-one planted problems, a twelve-rule catalogue,

10
00:00:34,691 --> 00:00:38,816
and an answer key sealed by hash on September twenty-fourth,

11
00:00:38,966 --> 00:00:40,953
before Bob saw any code.

12
00:00:41,103 --> 00:00:43,090
The organisers confirmed this preparation.

13
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:46,804
In Bob I built a custom mode, Clean Core Architect:

14
00:00:46,954 --> 00:00:50,519
a senior SAP architect that audits against the catalogue only,

15
00:00:50,669 --> 00:00:54,233
never invents a rule, and never claims something is verified

16
00:00:54,383 --> 00:00:56,833
on a system it has not seen.

17
00:00:56,983 --> 00:00:58,690
Read and edit tools only.

18
00:00:58,840 --> 00:01:00,313
One prompt per program.

19
00:01:00,463 --> 00:01:05,181
Bob reads the rules and the sample, then writes a JSON report;

20
00:01:05,331 --> 00:01:07,616
every write is approved by hand.

21
00:01:07,766 --> 00:01:10,861
Four audits cost zero point six six Bobcoin.

22
00:01:11,011 --> 00:01:15,730
Later, three programs were rewritten by three parallel sub-agents in sixteen minutes.

23
00:01:15,880 --> 00:01:19,310
This is Bob's output on the vendor ageing report.

24
00:01:19,460 --> 00:01:20,106
Problem three:

25
00:01:20,256 --> 00:01:23,289
raw database SQL that the cloud version forbids.

26
00:01:23,439 --> 00:01:24,084
Problem seven:

27
00:01:24,234 --> 00:01:28,858
Bob noticed the comment promises a currency conversion the code never does.

28
00:01:29,008 --> 00:01:32,837
And the right column lists what Bob could not verify,

29
00:01:32,987 --> 00:01:34,030
instead of guessing.

30
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:35,665
Against the sealed key:

31
00:01:35,815 --> 00:01:39,344
twenty-seven of twenty-nine rule problems, on the right lines.

32
00:01:39,494 --> 00:01:42,615
Ninety-one percent of the judged findings were right.

33
00:01:42,765 --> 00:01:44,250
Business logic is different:

34
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:45,476
one of twelve.

35
00:01:45,626 --> 00:01:50,382
Bob does not reason about runtime, and it does not pretend to.

36
00:01:50,532 --> 00:01:54,469
It never invented a rule, never claimed anything was verified,

37
00:01:54,619 --> 00:01:56,513
and asked before every write.

38
00:01:56,663 --> 00:02:01,010
That is exactly the behaviour you want from a first reviewer.

39
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:02,868
Then Bob rewrote one program:

40
00:02:03,018 --> 00:02:05,840
a data view, a class, seven unit tests.

41
00:02:05,990 --> 00:02:09,556
On a real SAP trial system the view failed on

42
00:02:09,706 --> 00:02:12,529
exactly the two objects Bob had marked candidate.

43
00:02:12,679 --> 00:02:16,616
With stand-in tables the class compiled and all seven tests passed.

44
00:02:16,766 --> 00:02:20,332
Then we compared the old rule with the new code

45
00:02:20,482 --> 00:02:22,933
for four hundred and thirty-one different ages,

46
00:02:23,083 --> 00:02:25,534
and planted a bug in a threshold:

47
00:02:25,684 --> 00:02:27,020
the tests caught it.

48
00:02:27,170 --> 00:02:28,964
This is the honest picture:

49
00:02:29,114 --> 00:02:32,463
four programs audited and scored, four rewritten, one tested,

50
00:02:32,613 --> 00:02:34,796
none verified on a customer's system.

51
00:02:34,946 --> 00:02:39,073
Every dashed cell is a claim we chose not to make.

52
00:02:39,223 --> 00:02:39,851
Total cost:

53
00:02:40,001 --> 00:02:41,795
about four of forty Bobcoin.

54
00:02:41,945 --> 00:02:43,739
Bob does the catalogue work;

55
00:02:43,889 --> 00:02:46,072
a person keeps the business decisions.

56
00:02:46,222 --> 00:02:49,960
Now we can say where the line is, with numbers.
